  "limitations": [
    "Composition Parts carry identity only: per-panel counts (3 rails, 3 metal inserts, 22 pickets, 4 U-channels) live in the authored dataset with recorded bases from the manufacturer material list, not in Part specs.",
    "Kit counts are manufacturer inventory statements (Tokens), not installed geometry: the U-channel length 39.5in equals the drawing-derived run height exactly; the picket stock length 43in implies 3.5in total seating, not a measured engagement.",
    "Receiving geometry (rail slot depth, picket seating depth, post rail-socket depth) remains absent: no source states them, so fitted cut lengths and engagement checks stay unvalidated.",
    "AssemblyStep publication awaits human review of the proposed master-install candidates; none publishes without it.",
    "The authored model candidate is excluded from models[] by the pending numeric provenance mapping (Amendment 008); its nulls publish as explicit gaps.",
    "Rail placements are drawing-derived authored choices from the CAD section chain; the datum interpretation is unconfirmed.",
    "The consumer infill fits one repeating cycle per panel: the upper picket run and its two U-channel segments are a recorded consumer-capability limitation.",
    "The model authors no post opinion: no post Part with citable values exists (the panel kit lists no posts; post specs exist at family level).",
    "Posts, caps and concrete are separate purchases: post-hole specs (12in diameter, 30-36in deep) come from the master install guide, not the panel kit."
  ],
  "lessons": [
    "Gap-closing round: the manufacturer's 8ft CAD page (retained as HTML through the corpus path with a new stdlib extractor) supplies the 8x6 panel's complete material list - 3 rails, 3 metal inserts (a previously unknown component), 4 U-channels at 1.25x1.5x39.5in (independently confirming the two-run count; the length closes exactly against the drawing's section chain), and 22 T&G pickets at 0.875x6x43in. Kit counts publish as Tokens; the picket 43-39.5=3.5in difference is implied seating, not a measured engagement."
  ],
  "proposed_improvements": [
    "Specsheet per-column panel weights and master-install post-hole specs are inspected and ready for a follow-up facts batch; the gate material lists on the same retained page supply socket-post specs."
  ],
